# Dhan Setu API: manual requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
# Click "Send Request" above any request. Run them top to bottom: later requests reuse
# tokens from earlier responses (e.g. {{login.response.body.$.tokens.access_token}}).
#
# OTP codes: the SMS sender is a stub, so the code is printed in the server log:
#   [SMS stub] verify_phone OTP for +91******3210: 123456
# Copy it into @otp below. Codes expire after 5 minutes.
# (With DEBUG=true in .env, responses also include the code as "dev_otp".)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api/v1
@email = you@example.com
@phone = 9876543210
@password = Secret123
@otp = 000000


### Health: process is up
GET {{baseUrl}}/health


### Readiness: PostgreSQL and Redis reachable
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready


### 1. Register: account starts as pending_verification and a code is "sent"
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "full_name": "Asha Verma",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


### 2. (Optional) Send a new code if the last one expired. One per number every 30 seconds.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/otp/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "purpose": "verify_phone"
}


### 3. Verify phone: activates the account and returns user + tokens. Set @otp first.
# @name verify
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "purpose": "verify_phone",
  "code": "{{otp}}"
}


### 4. Login with email or mobile number + password
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "{{phone}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


### 5. Current user (uses the access token from step 4)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.tokens.access_token}}


### 6. Update profile name
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.tokens.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "full_name": "Asha V."
}


### 7. Refresh: swaps the refresh token from step 4 for a new pair.
# The old refresh token stops working; sending this twice signs the session out (reuse detection).
# @name refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{login.response.body.$.tokens.refresh_token}}"
}


### 8. Logout: ends this device's session (uses the newest refresh token, from step 7)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refresh.response.body.$.refresh_token}}"
}


### ---- Login with OTP instead of password (account must be active)

### A. Send a login code
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/otp/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "purpose": "login"
}


### B. Verify the login code (set @otp to the new code first)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "purpose": "login",
  "code": "{{otp}}"
}


### ---- Cards (log in with step 4 first). A card is saved only after a ₹1 check.

### C1. Saved cards (default first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cards
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.tokens.access_token}}


### C2. Start adding a card: creates a ₹1 order. Use a NEW Idempotency-Key for each new card.
# @name cardCheck
POST {{baseUrl}}/cards/verifications
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.tokens.access_token}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}


### C3. Finish: send what Razorpay checkout returned (razorpay_payment_id, razorpay_signature).
# Needs PAYMENT_GATEWAY=razorpay and a real test-mode checkout; the mobile app does this.
POST {{baseUrl}}/cards/verifications/{{cardCheck.response.body.$.id}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.tokens.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "payment_id": "pay_REPLACE_ME",
  "signature": "REPLACE_WITH_64_HEX_CHARS"
}


### C4. Status of a card check
GET {{baseUrl}}/cards/verifications/{{cardCheck.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.tokens.access_token}}


### C5. Make a card the default (set @cardId first)
@cardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/cards/{{cardId}}/default
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.tokens.access_token}}


### C6. Remove a card (also deletes it at Razorpay)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/cards/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.tokens.access_token}}


### ---- Card payments (needs a saved card: set @cardId above)

### P1. Start a payment of ₹500 with a saved card. NEW Idempotency-Key per payment.
# @name payment
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.tokens.access_token}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount_paise": 50000,
  "card_id": "{{cardId}}",
  "description": "Test payment"
}


### P2. Verify: send what Razorpay checkout returned (the mobile app does this)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{payment.response.body.$.payment.id}}/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.tokens.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "payment_id": "pay_REPLACE_ME",
  "signature": "REPLACE_WITH_64_HEX_CHARS"
}


### P3. Payment status (poll while pending)
GET {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{payment.response.body.$.payment.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.tokens.access_token}}
